DSI command buffer below 4 GiB for real: the last page of the black scanout slot.

The DSI DMA address register is 32 bits and all of XNU's RAM is above 4 GiB on spes,
so the IOBufferMemoryDescriptor's address was truncated and the controller fetched some
other low page: all6 and all6nocpu (sweetpanel=1) reset early in userspace with no panic.
The buffer is now 0x90000000 + 11 * 16 MB + 16 MB - 4 KB (the 11 MB black frame leaves it
unused), mapped write-combined and filled with whole words; its address is logged.

